<html>
<head>
    <%- include("partials/header1.ejs") %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/css/styles.css">

    <style>

        /* Info card styling */
        .info-card {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 14px;
            border: 1px solid #E2E8F0;
            backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
            box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        h2 {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- Shared Navbar -->
    <%- include("partials/navbar.ejs") %>
     <!-- ⭐ UNIVERSAL Background -->
    <%- include('partials/globalBackground') %>

    <div class="residence-bg">

        <div class="content-box">

            <h2>Residence Class Visas</h2>
            <p>Explore New Zealand’s pathways to permanent residence and long-term settlement.</p>

            <div class="info-card">
                <a href="https://www.immigration.govt.nz/visas/skilled-migrant-category-resident-visa/"><h3>Skilled Migrant Category Resident Visa (SMC)</h3></a>
                <p>The Skilled Migrant Category (SMC) Resident Visa is a
                <strong>points-based residence pathway</strong> for people with skills that
                contribute to New Zealand’s economy.
                </p>

                <p>
                Applicants submit an <strong>Expression of Interest (EOI)</strong> and must meet
                the required points threshold. Points are awarded for factors such as
                <strong>skilled employment, income, qualifications, and experience</strong>.
                </p>

                <p>
                Successful applicants are granted <strong>residence</strong>, allowing them to
                live, work, and study in New Zealand indefinitely, subject to travel
                conditions.
                </p>

                <p>
                The SMC pathway is competitive and requires careful planning and
                <strong>accurate documentation</strong>.
                </p>

            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <a href="https://www.immigration.govt.nz/visas/straight-to-residence-visa/"><h3>Straight to Resident Visa</h3></a>
                <p>The Straight to Resident Visa provides a
                <strong>direct pathway to residence</strong> for people working in occupations
                listed on New Zealand’s <strong>Green List</strong>.
                </p>

                <p>
                Applicants must hold or have accepted a <strong>job offer</strong> in an eligible
                role and meet specific <strong>salary, registration, and skill requirements</strong>.
                </p>

                <p>
                This visa grants <strong>residence immediately</strong>, without requiring a
                prior period of work in New Zealand.
                </p>

                <p>
                Because Green List requirements are occupation-specific, applicants must
                ensure they meet <strong>all criteria precisely</strong>.
                </p>

            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <a href="https://www.immigration.govt.nz/visas/partner-of-a-new-zealander-resident-visa/"><h3>Partner of a New Zealander</h3></a>
                <p>The Partner of a New Zealander residence pathway is available to partners
                of <strong>New Zealand citizens or residents</strong>.
                </p>

                <p>
                Applicants must provide evidence of a
                <strong>genuine and stable relationship</strong>, such as shared finances,
                cohabitation, and social recognition.
                </p>

                <p>
                In many cases, applicants first hold a
                <strong>temporary partner-based visa</strong> before applying for residence.
                </p>

                <p>
                Applications are carefully assessed, and
                <strong>clear, consistent documentation</strong> is essential for approval.
                </p>

            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <a href="https://www.immigration.govt.nz/work/visas-for-investing-and-doing-business-in-new-zealand/"><h3>Investor Visas</h3></a>
                <p>Investor Visas are designed for individuals who can make a
                <strong>significant financial contribution</strong> to New Zealand’s economy.
                </p>

                <p>
                Applicants must invest a <strong>minimum required amount</strong> in acceptable
                New Zealand investments over a defined period.
                </p>

                <p>
                Ongoing <strong>compliance and investment maintenance</strong> is required for
                the duration of the visa conditions.
                </p>

                <p>
                These visas may provide a pathway to
                <strong>residence or permanent residence</strong> once all obligations are met.
                </p>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</body>
</html>
